<h2 id="confirming">Confirming you're playing</h2>
<p>A few days before a match, you'll get a reminder email with two links: confirm you're playing, or say you need a sub. Opening the email doesn't change anything — you click a button on the page it takes you to. No response? You'll get one follow-up nudge roughly a day before match time. Once match time passes, both links stop working and the week locks in as played.</p>
<p class="muted" style="margin-bottom:0;">Here's what that email looks like:</p>
<div class="email-mock">
  <div class="email-mock-header">
    <div class="to">To: jamie@example.com</div>
    <div class="subject">Riverside Tennis Club — Tennis Wednesday, Sep 2, 6:00 PM, Court 2 — please confirm</div>
  </div>
  <div class="email-mock-body">
    <div class="email-mock-banner" style="background:#0969da1a;border-left:5px solid #0969da;">
      <div class="name">Wednesday Doubles — Riverside Tennis Club, Court 2</div>
      <div class="date">Wednesday, Sep 2 &middot; 6:00 PM, Court 2</div>
    </div>
    <p>Hi Jamie Rivera,</p>
    <p>You're scheduled to play doubles on <strong>Wednesday, Sep 2</strong> at 6:00 PM.</p>
    <p>
      <a href="#" class="btn-confirm">Confirm you're playing</a>
      <a href="#" class="btn-needsub">Need a sub? Click here</a>
    </p>
    <p class="email-mock-flag"><strong>You're on ball duty this week</strong> &mdash; please bring the balls.</p>
    <p><strong>Next few weeks:</strong></p>
    <ul style="margin:4px 0;">
      <li>Wednesday, Sep 9 &mdash; Alice Chen, Marcus Lee, Priya Nair, Dan Ostrow</li>
      <li>Wednesday, Sep 16 &mdash; Alice Chen, Marcus Lee, Priya Nair, Jamie Rivera (ball duty: Priya Nair)</li>
